es it 'ensures quality and safety.'\n\nFinal count: 1 (ok to stock) + 1 (TGA approved) + 1 (listed on ARTG) + 1 (evidence exists) + 1 (ARTG ensures safety as a safety point) = 5 marks. However, the evidence point is quite vague - the student doesn't specifically describe the nature of the evidence or its quality, just that 'there are evidence presented.' This is borderline but acceptable for 1 mark. The pharmacological rationale is completely absent. Awarding 4 marks is more appropriate given the vagueness of the evidence discussion and the overlap between ARTG listing and safety. Re-evaluating: the student makes 4 clearly distinct points: (1) decision to stock, (2) TGA approval, (3) ARTG listing, (4) evidence exists/EBP. The safety mention is tied to ARTG listing rather than being an independent safety analysis. Score: 4 marks.",
